# Three.js Geometry Export to OBJ

## Overview
Exporting Three.js geometries and meshes to OBJ format for use in external 3D applications like Blender.

## Key Concepts

### Three.js Object Structure
- **Geometry**: Contains vertex positions, UV coordinates, normals, indices
- **Mesh**: A Geometry plus material and transformation (position, rotation, scale)
- **Group**: A container for multiple objects with local transforms
- **World Transform**: Converting from local to world space requires applying parent transforms

### Coordinate Systems
- **Three.js**: Y-up coordinate system (Y axis points up)
- **Blender**: Z-up coordinate system (Z axis points up)
- **Conversion**: Rotate -90° around X-axis to convert Y-up to Z-up

## API Reference

### Reading Geometry Data
```javascript
// Access vertex positions
const positionAttribute = geometry.getAttribute('position');
const positions = positionAttribute.array; // Float32Array

// Access face indices
const index = geometry.index;
const indices = index ? index.array : null;

// Get position at vertex i
const x = positions[i * 3];
const y = positions[i * 3 + 1];
const z = positions[i * 3 + 2];
```

### Working with Transforms
```javascript
import * as THREE from 'three';

// Create a matrix from position, rotation, scale
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
matrix.compose(position, quaternion, scale);

// Apply matrix to vector
const vector = new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z);
vector.applyMatrix4(matrix);

// Extract Euler angles from quaternion
const euler = new THREE.Euler().setFromQuaternion(quaternion);
```

### Coordinate Transformation
```javascript
// Rotate -90° around X-axis (Y-up to Z-up)
const rotationMatrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
rotationMatrix.makeRotationX(-Math.PI / 2); // -90 degrees

// Apply to vertex position
const position = new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z);
position.applyMatrix4(rotationMatrix);
```

## OBJ File Format

### Basic Structure
```
# Comment line
v x y z                    # Vertex position
vn x y z                   # Vertex normal
f v1/vt1/vn1 v2/vt2/vn2 v3/vt3/vn3  # Face (1-indexed)
```

### Writing Vertices and Faces
```javascript
let objContent = '';
const vertices = [];
const faces = [];

// Collect unique vertices
for (let i = 0; i < positions.length; i += 3) {
  vertices.push(`v ${positions[i]} ${positions[i+1]} ${positions[i+2]}`);
}

// Write faces (OBJ uses 1-based indexing)
for (let i = 0; i < indices.length; i += 3) {
  const i1 = indices[i] + 1;
  const i2 = indices[i+1] + 1;
  const i3 = indices[i+2] + 1;
  faces.push(`f ${i1} ${i2} ${i3}`);
}

objContent = vertices.join('\n') + '\n' + faces.join('\n');
```

## Common Patterns

### Handling Groups and Hierarchies
```javascript
function traverseScene(object, callback) {
  callback(object);
  object.children.forEach(child => traverseScene(child, callback));
}
```

### Flattening Transforms
```javascript
// For each mesh, compute world position and rotation
const worldMatrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
object.updateMatrixWorld();
worldMatrix.copy(object.matrixWorld);
```

## File I/O in Node.js

### Writing OBJ Files
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
fs.writeFileSync('/path/to/file.obj', objContent, 'utf-8');
```

## Related Tools
- **Three.js OBJExporter**: Built-in exporter (limited)
- **Babylon.js**: Alternative with better export features
- **glTF**: Modern 3D format with better support for transforms

