# Three.js InstancedMesh Handling and Flattening

## Overview
Working with Three.js InstancedMesh objects, which use instancing to render many copies of the same geometry efficiently. Exporting InstancedMesh requires flattening instances into individual geometries.

## InstancedMesh Basics

### What is InstancedMesh?
```javascript
const geometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(1, 1, 1);
const material = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial();
const instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, 100);

// Set instance transforms via matrices
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
  matrix.makeTranslation(i * 2, 0, 0);
  instancedMesh.setMatrixAt(i, matrix);
}
instancedMesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
```

### Key Properties
- `count`: Number of instances
- `instanceMatrix`: Contains the matrix for each instance
- `instanceColor`: Optional per-instance colors

## Extracting Instance Data

### Reading Instance Matrices
```javascript
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);

// Extract position
const position = new THREE.Vector3();
position.setFromMatrixPosition(matrix);

// Extract rotation
const quaternion = new THREE.Quaternion();
matrix.decompose(position, quaternion, new THREE.Vector3());

// Extract scale
const scale = new THREE.Vector3();
matrix.decompose(new THREE.Vector3(), new THREE.Quaternion(), scale);
```

## Flattening to Standard Meshes

### Full Flattening Process
```javascript
function flattenInstancedMesh(instancedMesh) {
  const meshes = [];
  const baseGeometry = instancedMesh.geometry;
  const material = instancedMesh.material;

  for (let i = 0; i < instancedMesh.count; i++) {
    // Get instance matrix
    const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
    instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);

    // Clone geometry
    const geometry = baseGeometry.clone();

    // Apply instance transform to all vertices
    const posAttribute = geometry.getAttribute('position');
    const positions = posAttribute.array;
    const vertex = new THREE.Vector3();

    for (let j = 0; j < positions.length; j += 3) {
      vertex.set(positions[j], positions[j+1], positions[j+2]);
      vertex.applyMatrix4(matrix);
      positions[j] = vertex.x;
      positions[j+1] = vertex.y;
      positions[j+2] = vertex.z;
    }
    posAttribute.needsUpdate = true;

    // Create mesh
    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);
    meshes.push(mesh);
  }

  return meshes;
}
```

### Adding to Scene
```javascript
const flatMeshes = flattenInstancedMesh(instancedMesh);
flatMeshes.forEach(mesh => {
  parent.add(mesh);
  // or process for export
});
```

## Exporting InstancedMesh

### Strategy 1: Flatten Then Export
```javascript
function exportInstancedMesh(instancedMesh, objExporter) {
  const meshes = flattenInstancedMesh(instancedMesh);
  const group = new THREE.Group();
  meshes.forEach(mesh => group.add(mesh));
  return objExporter.parse(group);
}
```

### Strategy 2: Direct Export with Accumulation
```javascript
function accumulateGeometries(instancedMesh, worldMatrix = null) {
  const baseGeometry = instancedMesh.geometry;
  const vertices = [];
  const faces = [];
  let vertexOffset = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < instancedMesh.count; i++) {
    const instanceMatrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
    instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, instanceMatrix);

    // Apply world transform if needed
    if (worldMatrix) {
      instanceMatrix.multiplyMatrices(worldMatrix, instanceMatrix);
    }

    // Get base geometry data
    const posAttr = baseGeometry.getAttribute('position');
    const positions = posAttr.array;
    const index = baseGeometry.index;

    // Transform and add vertices
    const vertex = new THREE.Vector3();
    for (let j = 0; j < positions.length; j += 3) {
      vertex.set(positions[j], positions[j+1], positions[j+2]);
      vertex.applyMatrix4(instanceMatrix);
      vertices.push(vertex.x, vertex.y, vertex.z);
    }

    // Add faces with offset
    if (index) {
      const indices = index.array;
      for (let j = 0; j < indices.length; j += 3) {
        const i1 = indices[j] + vertexOffset;
        const i2 = indices[j+1] + vertexOffset;
        const i3 = indices[j+2] + vertexOffset;
        faces.push(i1, i2, i3);
      }
    } else {
      // Non-indexed geometry
      const vertexCount = positions.length / 3;
      for (let j = 0; j < vertexCount; j += 3) {
        faces.push(
          j + vertexOffset,
          j+1 + vertexOffset,
          j+2 + vertexOffset
        );
      }
    }

    vertexOffset += positions.length / 3;
  }

  return { vertices, faces };
}
```

## Memory Considerations

### When to Flatten
- **Do flatten**: When exporting to formats that don't support instancing
- **Don't flatten**: When memory is critical and you're processing for display

### Efficient Flattening
```javascript
// Reuse buffers to reduce allocation
const scratchGeometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
const vertex = new THREE.Vector3();
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
```

## Testing and Validation

### Verify Flattening
```javascript
// Check that flattened meshes match original positions
const flatMeshes = flattenInstancedMesh(instancedMesh);

console.log(`Original count: ${instancedMesh.count}`);
console.log(`Flattened meshes: ${flatMeshes.length}`);

// Spot check first and last instance
const matrix0 = new THREE.Matrix4();
instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(0, matrix0);
console.log('Instance 0 position:', matrix0.elements.slice(12, 15));

const pos0 = flatMeshes[0].geometry.getAttribute('position');
console.log('Flattened 0 vertices:', Array.from(pos0.array).slice(0, 3));
```

## Related Concepts
- BufferGeometry for efficient geometry storage
- Matrix4 for 3D transformations
- Batch rendering vs instancing trade-offs
- Normal vector transformation with transforms

